<p>In the latest turn, Iran kept impeding traffic through the Strait of Hormuz on March 27-28 while continuing to trade strikes with Israel, and the Trump administration said it was waiting for Tehran&#x27;s formal response to a 15-point peace proposal. U.S. and Iranian accounts sharply diverged: CBS reported that President Trump said Iran had let 10 ships pass and that talks were underway, while Iran&#x27;s Revolutionary Guards said the strait was closed and warned of a severe response to any ship attempting to transit. The disruption matters far beyond the battlefield because the Strait of Hormuz is one of the world&#x27;s most important oil-shipping routes, and Iranian lawmakers were also weighing whether to formalize tolls for passage after ships were turned back. The broader conflict widened as well, with reports that attacks struck Iranian nuclear facilities and industrial sites and that U.S. troops in Saudi Arabia came under attack, while President Trump said Iran must reopen the strait to all traffic by April 6 or face the destruction of its energy plants. Even with tensions rising, diplomacy remains part of the story, with Washington still pressing for a negotiated outcome.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/nvbTXDqESvHm6NLjVGRIbFih1SaOZDwarRK1RKXOTlFrvBVRQ2L15ZOX6HjpIFFgNkQSLz0oy8QMKbYGhGGVXfuizrDYZ63t6y42iXuYW2d7d_I1O0oOwi5k7Uq3YoJvHhyeQN3MWmmrDFxs4QSHVY0OmTs61U8cUew7X8lb3EPsjatZPX9yN98rGz0tQogITuFZ7JOrtN3mSeg-x644RvM7p35kUDwj7ZMF_g' alt='Iran has effectively cut off traffic through the Strait of Hormuz, leaving thousands of vessels idling on either side of it.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Immediate compliance: Two ships turned back on Friday after being warned not to pass through the strait, showing that Iran&#x27;s warnings were already changing ship movements in real time.</li><li>Gridlock beyond tankers: The New York Times reported that container ships were also turned back and that thousands of vessels were idling on either side of Hormuz as traffic seized up.</li><li>Second chokepoint: Iran also threatened the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, raising fears that disruption could spread from the Gulf to the Red Sea route.</li><li>Naming remark: President Trump briefly referred to the waterway as the &quot;Strait of Trump&quot; and said the slip was a &quot;mistake&quot;.</li></ul><blockquote>There&#x27;s no accidents with me. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: President Trump said reopening the route to oil traffic was a prerequisite for a peace deal, showing that Washington is tying its public push for negotiations to a concrete maritime demand. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/strait-trump-us-president-says-iran-must-open-key-waterway'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iran&#x27;s Revolutionary Guards: The Guards said the Strait of Hormuz is closed and warned of a severe response to any ship that tries to pass, directly rejecting Trump&#x27;s suggestion that Iran is selectively allowing transit. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/iran-claims-strait-of-hormuz-is-closed-as-trump-says-talks-are-underway/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Iranian officials: Tehran said strikes inside the country hit a uranium processing plant and industrial sites, underscoring the damage Iran says it is absorbing as the war widens. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/27/world/middleeast/iran-israel-us-rubio-war.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-strait-of-hormuz-oil-tanker-israel/'>Iran war rages, Strait of Hormuz still blocked as Trump pushes for a deal</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-israel-war-highlights-west-asia-conflict-march-27-2026/article70790939.ece'>Iran-Israel war highlights: Attacks ramp up in Iran war including strikes on Iranian nuclear facilities and U.S. troops in Saudi</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/strait-trump-us-president-says-iran-must-open-key-waterway'>&#x27;Strait of Trump&#x27;: US president says Iran must open key waterway</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/27/world/middleeast/iran-israel-us-rubio-war.html'>Iran Moves to Assert Control Over Strait While Trading Strikes With Israel</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>